# nvn/textures: the no-BC path is on by itself on a GPU without BC, and decodes BC1-5 on the GPU at upload (kernel bcd); DM_TEST_NO_BC, DM_NO_BC_GPU
#
# Source:    https://github.com/mianmuhammadse/nxnative  branch no-bc (a community fork of seedds/nxnative), commits 6804e174 ("Restore the no-BC decompression path (iPhone 15 / A16 and
#            other GPUs without BC)"), 5b3a5c7b + 30198611 + 8e2beb9b (upload batch order: zero fills, barrier, GPU jobs, barrier, copies; encoder-stage barriers, counted), 9d90f356 (log)
# Author:    Mian Muhammad (the commits' author)
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE; the fork keeps it). The attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# Why: A14-A16 iPhones (iPhone 12 to 15 non-Pro) have Metal 4 but no BC texture formats. Our tree already decoded BC on the CPU there (NX2Apple 0063 / 0064 = our 0410 / 0411, nvn_bcdec.c),
#   but only when the game's profile said tex_bc_cpu, and every texture went through the CPU deswizzle plus the CPU decode (the fork measured over 300 ms in one frame of an A16).
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m; tests t_bc_cpu, t_nobc_order):
#   1. g_bc_cpu (the no-BC path) = !supportsBCTextureCompression, whatever the profile says: tex_bc_cpu is still read and accepted, and no longer needed (the app's DM_PROF_TEX_BC_CPU=1
#      changes nothing now). DM_TEST_NO_BC=1 forces the path on a GPU that has BC (the Mac; the tests use it). The MDIE for a no-BC device stays only for a path turned off (unreachable).
#   2. A BC1-5 2D-type texture (2D, 2D array, cube, 1D) that is not 3D, multisample, linear or in a sparse pool is deswizzled on the GPU as any other texture, and decoded on the GPU at the
#      upload batch's flush: kernel bcd (from the fork, runtime-compiled MSL), one thread per 4x4 block, writing a 2D view of the level and layer in the decompressed format (an sRGB
#      RGBA8 texture through an RGBA8Unorm view, raw values). Such textures get ShaderWrite | PixelFormatView usage. BC6H / BC7 / 3D / sparse / linear textures and buffer→texture copies
#      keep the CPU decode of 0410 / 0411; DM_NO_BC_GPU=0 sends every BC texture there (the reference, our behaviour before this patch). mip skip (0501), partial re-uploads, the big-pool
#      source buffers work with it (same loop); the direct GPU upload stays off for BC (as before).
#   3. up_flush, only when the batch holds no-BC jobs: zero fills first, an encoder-stage barrier, the jobs, an encoder-stage barrier, then every other copy in its order (g_up_ebar counts
#      them). A batch without jobs (always so on a GPU with BC) is encoded exactly as before; tex_zero_fill marks its copies (up_blit.fill), which only that order reads.
#   4. copy_t2t: an ASTC 4x4 source into a decompressed (RGBA8) BC texture of the same size goes through a compute kernel that reads the texels and writes them (a2u, from the fork; sRGB
#      re-encoded), as the Switch's raw block copy would read in the destination format.
#   5. Compressed-alias pairs (bcp_*, DM_NVN_BC_ALIAS) are off without BC (their block copies would move decoded texels as blocks), as in the fork.
#   6. The memory line says how many BC textures took the GPU / CPU decode. RED_ONCE table raised to 190 (key 180 is new).
# On a GPU with BC (A17 Pro and later, M1 and later): g_bc_cpu is 0, so bc_gdec_tex() is 0, no job is ever queued, ndisp is 0 in up_flush, tex_desc adds no usage, bcp_on() is unchanged:
#   no behaviour change (t_bc_astc of 0511 checks it with g_bc_cpu 0).
# Adapted from the fork: its base is 195 upstream commits newer than ours (it re-adds the whole no-BC path upstream had removed, 14fbcf9); here the existing CPU path (g_bc_cpu, 0410 / 0411)
#   is kept and the GPU decode is added into our pkg_upload_ (which has mip skip, partial re-uploads, big-pool sources, sparse gathers) and our up_flush (whose copies carry t2b / tsrc /
#   bar). Fork pieces not taken: its no_bc() / bc_unpack() (ours is g_bc_cpu + nvn_bc_unpacked), its attach() change (ours already attaches decompressed BC textures, t_bc_cpu checks it),
#   its copy_b2t CPU decode (ours exists, parallel), its readback refusals (ours exist, red lines 95 and the t2b one).
# Defaults: on by itself on a no-BC GPU. Env: DM_TEST_NO_BC=1 (test), DM_NO_BC_GPU=0 (CPU decode only).
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad).
# Tests (M1 Pro, macOS, DM_TEST_NO_BC=1 or g_bc_cpu forced): t_bc_cpu (extended: its uploads run with the GPU decode and with the CPU decode, and random blocks of every BC1-5 format
#   through the GPU decode match bcdec within 1 level) 796/0 under MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1; t_nobc_order (new) A + B 6/0. NOT run on an A14-A16 device.

